    "paras": [
     "Liolaemus aparicioi is a species of lizard in the family  Liolaemidae. The species is endemic to Bolivia."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Etymology",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "The specific name, aparicioi, is in honor of Bolivian herpetologist James Aparicio Effen."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Geographic range",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "L. aparicioi is found in western Bolivia, in La Paz Department."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Habitat",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "The preferred natural habitat of L. aparicioi is dry forest, at altitudes of 3,000–3,900 m (9,800–12,800 ft)."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Description",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "Small for its genus, L. aparicio may attain a snout-to-vent length (SVL) of about 6 cm (2.4 in), with a tail length almost twice SVL."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Behavior",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "L. aparicioi is terrestrial."
    ]
   },
